<title>USA: Alaskans vote against cruise passenger tax.</title>
<headline>Alaskans vote against cruise passenger tax.</headline>
<dateline>ANCHORAGE, Alaska 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A ballot measure that would have imposed a $7-per-passenger fee on cruise ships docking in Alaska's capital city was defeated by voters, Juneau city officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Forty-six percent of voters casting ballots in Tuesday's city election approved of the measure, while 54 percent opposed it.</p>
<p>The issue was put to a vote after petitions were gathered this summer by local residents worried about rapidly growing cruise ship crowds.</p>
<p>Advocates of the fee said it would help offset the costs of providing police, safety and other services for the more than 400,000 cruise ship passengers who visit Juneau each summer. Cruise ship and tourism companies were opposed.</p>
